{#- The press, for a quote made somewhere targum has no page (targum-internal#80).

    In the chat a quote becomes a card in the thread, and the card's button posts
    `/build`. Over a connector the quote is made in somebody else's app, so it comes back
    as a link to this: the same quote, the same button, the same `/build`, on a page of
    ours. `Handler._build` remains the only path to `Library.claim`, and the model still
    cannot press anything.

    It is the sign-in family's furniture — the lockup, one card, no navigation — for the
    reason that page gives: somebody is in the middle of something that started
    elsewhere, and three ways off this page would be three ways to lose them.

    §6 governs the words. A wait is said in minutes and a cost in credits — one credit is
    one minute of audio or video (§12, 2026-09-23) — and never as a price: this page never
    prints what the job cost to make. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('signin.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="signin">
<main class="gate">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
    <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
      <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span>targum</span>
  </a>

  <div class="door">
  {% if job.reader %}
    {#- Already built, which is what a second visit to the same link looks like. Not an
        error, and the way on is the reader itself. -#}
    <h1>{{ t("press.page.this-one-is-ready", "This one is ready") }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ job.title }}</p>
    <form method="get" action="/reader/{{ job.reader }}">
      <button class="go" type="submit"><span class="go-says">{{ t("press.page.open-it", "Open it") }}</span><svg class="go-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></button>
    </form>

  {% elif job.stage in ('working', 'reading') %}
    {#- Pressed, and being made. Reached two ways: without script, where the press
        redirects back here and the way on is the button; and **with** script, where the
        reader simply reloaded or came back to the link while it built. That second way
        used to dead-end — the watcher looked for the press form, which this state has
        not got, so the page never polled and never opened the reader (2026-09-23). The
        watch hangs off its own element, present in both states, so coming back to the
        tab is the same as never having left it. -#}
    <h1>{{ t("press.page.we-re-making-it", "We're making it") }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ job.title }}</p>
    <div id="press-watch" data-job="{{ job.id }}" data-made="{{ job.made|int }}"
         data-usually="{{ job.usually|round|int }}"></div>
    <p class="said" id="press-doing" role="status">{{ job.message or t("press.page.getting-started", "Getting started.") }}</p>
    <p class="said" id="press-left" role="status"></p>
    <form method="get" action="/build/{{ job.id }}">
      <button class="go" type="submit">{{ t("press.page.see-how-it-s-going", "See how it's going") }}</button>
    </form>
    <p class="aside">{{ t("press.page.it-s-also-on-your-texts", "It's on your texts too, and we'll open it here when it's ready.") }}
      <a href="/texts">{{ t("press.page.go-to-your-texts", "Go to your texts") }}</a></p>

  {% elif job.stage == 'ready' %}
    <h1>{{ job.title }}</h1>
    {%- if job.english %}<p class="said">{{ job.english }}</p>{% endif %}
    <ul class="scopes">
      {#- `usually` is seconds — `Library._how_long` says so. It was rendered as minutes
          here, which promised "about 420 minutes" for a seven-minute build. -#}
      {%- if job.usually and job.usually >= 30 %}
      {#- The quote's guess, from what builds of this shape took here lately. It is put
          away the moment the press lands, because from then on the page is watching this
          build and can say something truer: a 68-chapter text was quoted a minute, and
          the card went on saying "Ready in about 1 minute" while the line under it said
          this was taking longer than usual (2026-09-23). Two numbers about the same wait,
          disagreeing, on one card. -#}
      <li id="press-quoted"><span class="scope-says">{{ tn("press.page.ready-in-about-minutes", (job.usually / 60)|round|int, "Ready in about {n} minute", "Ready in about {n} minutes") }}</span></li>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if job.known_line %}
      <li><span class="scope-says">{{ job.known_line }}</span></li>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if job.audio %}
      {#- A cost is credits since 2026-09-23 (§12), and a credit is a minute of audio or
          video. This line read "Uses 1 minutes of your hours" for a one-minute video,
          which is the whole reason the vocabulary changed; the rate lives beside the
          balance, so a cost point says the figure alone. -#}
      <li>
        <span class="scope-says">{{ t("press.page.it-has-audio", "It has audio") }}</span>
        <span class="scope-cost">{{ tn("press.page.uses-credits", (job.seconds / 60)|round|int, "Uses {n} credit", "Uses {n} credits") }}</span>
      </li>
      {%- endif %}
    </ul>
    <form method="post" action="/build/{{ job.id }}" id="press" data-job="{{ job.id }}"
          data-usually="{{ job.usually|round|int }}">
      <button class="go" type="submit"><span class="go-says">{{ t("press.page.read-this", "Read this") }}</span><svg class="go-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></button>
    </form>
    <p class="said" id="press-doing" role="status" hidden></p>
    <p class="said" id="press-left" role="status" hidden></p>
    {#- Said before the press, and replaced by the way out once it is pressed: until then
        "go to your texts" would be pointing at a text that is not there. -#}
    <p class="aside" id="press-note">{{ t("press.page.you-asked-for-this-somewhere-else", "You asked for this somewhere else. Nothing has been made yet.") }}</p>
    <p class="aside" id="press-away" hidden>{{ t("press.page.it-s-also-on-your-texts", "It's on your texts too, and we'll open it here when it's ready.") }}
      <a href="/texts">{{ t("press.page.go-to-your-texts", "Go to your texts") }}</a></p>

  {% else %}
    <h1>{{ t("press.page.we-can-t-make-this-one", "We can't make this one") }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ job.error or job.blocked or t("press.page.that-quote-has-gone-stale", "That quote has gone stale. Ask again where you asked before.") }}</p>
    <p class="aside"><a href="/">{{ t("press.page.go-to-your-texts", "Go to your texts") }}</a></p>
  {% endif %}
  </div>
</main>
{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('press.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
